---
title: "Drawbridge — Review state machine: the system refuses to guess"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB
  [*] --> INTAKE

  INTAKE --> QUESTIONNAIRE_OUT : plan checkpointed
  QUESTIONNAIRE_OUT --> GATED : gate_scope contact · P1 blocks the send without a token
  GATED --> QUESTIONNAIRE_OUT : contact authorised, single-use token spent
  QUESTIONNAIRE_OUT --> REPLIES_IN : coverage reaches 90 percent
  REPLIES_IN --> EVIDENCE_REVIEW : documents screened and stamped
  EVIDENCE_REVIEW --> SCORED : findings reconciled
  SCORED --> GATED : gate_scope decision · memo written, waiting on gate G1
  GATED --> DECIDED : signed approval token, identity recorded
  DECIDED --> MONITORED : watchdog takes over the vendor
  MONITORED --> MONITORED : scheduled sweep, no signal

  MONITORED --> EVIDENCE_REVIEW : high-confidence watchdog.hit opens a NEW linked review

  REPLIES_IN --> QUESTIONNAIRE_OUT : re-tier · evidence widens the declared data scope
  EVIDENCE_REVIEW --> QUESTIONNAIRE_OUT : re-tier · the additional domain's questions go out

  INTAKE --> NEEDS_HUMAN
  QUESTIONNAIRE_OUT --> NEEDS_HUMAN : three chases, no reply
  REPLIES_IN --> NEEDS_HUMAN : answer below the confidence threshold
  EVIDENCE_REVIEW --> NEEDS_HUMAN : corrupt or unreadable document
  SCORED --> NEEDS_HUMAN : invalid transition, DLQ exhaustion or output screening
  GATED --> NEEDS_HUMAN : the gate cannot be resolved
  DECIDED --> NEEDS_HUMAN : an event arrives that a decided review may not absorb
  MONITORED --> NEEDS_HUMAN : a signal needs triage rather than a re-review

  NEEDS_HUMAN --> [*] : analyst resolves and the review resumes

  note right of GATED
    One state, two scopes.
    gate_scope = contact  → human gate G2, first outbound
                            email, enforced by policy P1
    gate_scope = decision → human gate G1, risk acceptance
    Gates are what a person does; policies are what the
    chokepoint enforces. Both tokens are signed, single-use
    and scoped, and both are verified at the gateway with a
    PUBLIC key — never in the user interface, and never with
    a key the gateway could sign with.
  end note

  note right of NEEDS_HUMAN
    Enterable from any state.
    Parks the review with a dashboard card
    explaining what stalled and why.
    It never silently corrects.
  end note

  note left of MONITORED
    History is never mutated.
    A reopened review is a new record
    linked to the old one, so the
    audit trail stays intact.
  end note

  note left of EVIDENCE_REVIEW
    Re-tiering is the one legitimate backward
    move inside a single review. Tier only ever
    goes UP — a downward re-tier is an attack
    surface. Every change increments plan_version
    and writes a TierChange naming the evidence.
  end note
